    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "I maintain the unibilum package on Alpine Linux. I upgraded the package late last week. I didn't at first connect the unibilium upgrade to an issue that started happening when I would exit neovim, that the cursor remains in blink mode. I found a number of issues on the neovim tracker about what seemed like the same or similar issues. First I built neovim 0.12.5. When that didn't help, I back ported https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/a3eff66e313b89cf721ad70ea34c41b7425200c1 and added that to my build, but still no joy. So I tried another tack and rolled my local install of unibilium back to 2.1.2. The rollback made the nvim cursor blink on exit no longer happen. So I bisected v2.1.2 to v2.1.4. The resulting suspect commit is https://github.com/neovim/unibilium/commit/1436391cc8192c35ba90910948921c6a1a02cf56. After rebuilding unibilum 2.1.4 with 1436391 revert patch and installing, the issue no longer happens. I realize that that commit in and of itself does not seem like a likely candidate for the issue. I would have thought that reading the complete terminfo file would have helped. Obviously, I still need to debug this further with strace and ltrace. But I wanted to get a starting point for trying to find a fix.\n\n",
